cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this repository when using its proofs, exposition, or verification code."
title: "The Backaction Cost of Causal Threshold Measurements"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lin
    given-names: Ruge
    email: gogoko699@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/GoGoKo699/Causal-Threshold-Backaction"
url: "https://github.com/GoGoKo699/Causal-Threshold-Backaction"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Research exposition, complete proofs, a finite distributed apparatus, and
  reproducible calculations for the entropy cost of causal threshold measurements.
  Under exact calibration and preservation of every charge sector, the optimal
  pure-input cost is determined up to universal additive constants by coarse-charge
  entropy. General-instrument results treat imperfect preservation, calibration,
  and causality under explicit assumptions.
keywords:
  - quantum measurement
  - causality
  - entropy
  - quantum information
  - threshold measurement
